[E-TYPE-MISMATCH] Error: type mismatch
   ╭─[ reject/lambda-implicit-mode-mismatch.sw:6:22 ]
   │
 6 │ def f: Nat -> Nat := [a: Type] (x: a) => x
   │                      ──────────┬──────────  
   │                                ╰──────────── this lambda takes an implicit parameter first, but the expected type `Nat -> Nat` takes an explicit one
   │ 
   │ Note: a lambda takes its expected type's parameters in order: `[a: …]` takes `[a: …] -> …`, `[auto h: …]` takes `[auto h: …] -> …`, and `x` or `(x: …)` takes `(x: …) -> …` (with implicit ones in front of it introduced for you)
───╯
